-- Frozen migration-0001 seed written through the HTTP API. The baseline test
-- loads it at migration 0001 and applies all remaining embedded migrations.
-- The supported household schema has its own fixture, household_0016_seed.sql.
-- Rebased for #405 on 2026-10-26 without changing original financial facts.
-- Reviewed for #192's whole-value canonical CHECKs (2026-10-12): its exact
-- coefficient data remains valid without changing any financial figures.
-- Reviewed for #148's required opening operation/source journal (2026-10-13):
-- every seeded lot already names both; financial rows and IDs are unchanged.
-- Reviewed for #573's single-book triggers (2026-11-18): the one book is id 1
-- and only its default currency is updated later, so it loads unchanged.
-- Reviewed for the calendar-date CHECKs in #584 and #635: the fixture passes
-- the rewritten baseline without changes to its dates or financial rows.
--
-- It is frozen on purpose. Regenerating it against a later schema would defeat
-- the test: the point is to migrate data written by the OLD app, which future
-- app code may no longer be able to produce. Add a second seed for a later
-- release rather than editing this one.
--
-- Excluded: rows the migration inserts itself (account_kinds,
-- market_data_sources, setup_steps), goose's own bookkeeping, and the FTS5
-- shadow tables, which the triggers rebuild from the base rows below.
--
-- Two ordering accommodations, because a dump is in table order and a book is
-- not a tree: the loader defers foreign keys to COMMIT, and the book's default
-- currency is set at the end, once the commodity it points at exists. That one
-- cannot be deferred, because a trigger checks it on write and triggers do not
-- honour defer_foreign_keys.
-- #393 recorded shape of the existing gross dividend; no payer is invented.

UPDATE books SET default_currency_commodity_id = 1 WHERE id = 1;
